# Job 8: how much of a distro build's gain is -O2 rather than LTO.
# A is master 856d23b9e as it builds today (-O). B is the same tree plus
# patches/cflags-o2.diff: -O2 added after the -O line of auto/cc/test (line 74
# in the gcc branch, line 118 in the clang branch). The last -O on the command
# line wins; build/Makefile then shows "-O -O2". The explicit
# -fno-strict-aliasing stays in force: gcc 15.2 reports -fstrict-aliasing
# [disabled] for "-O -fno-strict-aliasing -O2" (checked locally).
# How the patch is applied, the lab image and the reasons for the empty FUNCS
# and for STRACE=0 are in the header of job 07.
# Local build, gcc 15.2: unitd text grows from 506706 to 540326 bytes at -O2.
# The share of -O2 is this delta. Job 07 gives the LTO share at -O, job 09 the
# LTO share at -O2. The two do not add up; read the three deltas as separate
# measurements. PRIMARY is r_instructions; s_instructions has the PHP engine in
# it, which -O2 does not touch.
JOB=08-o2-hello
REV_A=856d23b9ed2cecbd96d5452cf790f828fc55d700
REV_B=856d23b9ed2cecbd96d5452cf790f828fc55d700
PATCH_B=patches/cflags-o2.diff
WORKLOAD=hello
CONNS=6
WARM=2
DUR=8
REPS=4
PERF=1
PRIMARY=r_instructions
EXPECT=r_instructions lower in B by more than the null band (guess before any run: 2 to 6 percent); s_instructions lower by less; ok equal, bad 0, alerts 0; unitd_b in meta.txt differs from unitd_a
FALSIFY=r_instructions NO CLAIM or NOISY, or higher in B: -O2 gives nothing this lab can resolve at hello.php c=6; or build/Makefile of B has no -O2: the patch did not reach the build
